    <DataNode elementId="AT3G14940-MONOMER" textLabel="Phosphoenolpyruvate carboxylase 3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q84VW9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="695" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Phosphoenolpyruvate carboxylase (PEPC) is an enzyme often associated with photosynthesis in C4 plants such as |FRAME: TAX-4577 &lt;i&gt;Zea mays&lt;/i&gt;| (see |FRAME: CPLX-846 ZmPEPC|). However, in C3 plants, such as |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col|, this enzyme may also play a role in several processes such as replenishing depleted |FRAME: PWY-5690 TCA cycle| compounds that have been used for nitrogen assimilation or providing carbon skeletons for |FRAME: PWY-6549 nitrogen remobilization| during senescence |CITS: [17894783][20202167]|. There are two types of PEPCs found in plants. This PPC3 enzyme is one of three &quot;plant-type PEPCs&quot; found in |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col|. Overexpression of this enzyme in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; increased the PEP carboxylase activity of the extract indicating that this protein does have catalytic activty |CITS: [17894783]|. Interestingly, PPC3 and the other plant-type PEPCs may interact with with bacterial-type PEPCs to form complexes that allow PEPC activity to persist under conditions that would normally inhibit plant-type PEPC activity |CITS: [20202167]|. Arabidopsis has one bacterial-type PEPC, &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.arabidopsis.org/servlets/TairObject?id=27572&amp;type=locus&quot;&gt;PPC4&lt;/A&gt;. When expressed alone in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; this protein had no PEPC activity |CITS: [17894783]|. However, when the RcPPC4 ortholog from |FRAME: TAX-3988 &lt;i&gt;Ricinus communis&lt;/i&gt;| (castor bean) was incubated with PPC3 from Arabidopsis, an active heterooligomeric complex with novel PEPC enzymatic properties was generated |CITS: [20202167]|. This supports the previous finding of this type of heterooligomeric complex &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; in castor bean |CITS: [17894783]|. Further work will be required to determine if a similar complex is formed in Arabidopsis, and, if so, what its enzymatic properties and biological significance are.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G14940-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G14940.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q84VW9" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtPPC3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="PEPC 3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="PEPCase 3" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-18104" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G14940.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":AMBIGUOUS" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G14940" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17894783" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20202167" />
    </DataNode>
